1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:10,000
The KRITIS-Dachgesetz has applied since March, the new BSIG since December.

2
00:00:10,000 --> 00:00:20,000
A waterworks must meet both. This platform brings them together. I sign in as the GRC Manager.

3
00:00:20,000 --> 00:00:33,000
The overview shows the state per law and facility, the next deadlines and the residual risk matrix.

4
00:00:33,000 --> 00:00:45,000
The deadlines are projected: the Registration is still planned, as the thresholds ordinance isn't in force yet.

5
00:00:45,000 --> 00:01:00,000
In the cockpit I open the resilience measures under § 13 for Wasserwerk Nord.

6
00:01:00,000 --> 00:01:15,000
The backup power is already proven for the BSIG. I refer to that work and upload the test report.

7
00:01:15,000 --> 00:01:30,000
I set the status to "implemented". The risk engine recalculates the residual risk.

8
00:01:30,000 --> 00:01:45,000
The power outage leaves the critical area. If the engine is down, the rating is pending and retried automatically.

9
00:01:45,000 --> 00:02:00,000
Under "Approvals" the AI's suggestions wait. The AI only ever sees the public statute text.

10
00:02:00,000 --> 00:02:15,000
A suggestion counts only once a person approves it, and nobody approves their own Risk Assessment.

11
00:02:15,000 --> 00:02:30,000
Now as the Auditor, who sees everything and changes nothing.

12
00:02:30,000 --> 00:02:45,000
The Activity Log shows every change: who, when, from which value to which. The database forbids editing it.

13
00:02:45,000 --> 00:03:00,000
Every organization is isolated twice, in the application and in the database. Thanks for watching.
